## Deviations / judgment calls (none forced by ambiguity in stubs, all consistent with documented design)

- `unmergeable` items (`update attractor/component/term/persona`) are surfaced through the same errors textarea + error-list as parse errors, using their `item.raw` text and a synthetic message — the stub comment said "re-show as an error," and no test exercises this path, so this is the simplest reading consistent with the design notes.
- Primary textarea is unconditionally cleared after both Run and Retry (not conditioned on "at least one success") — simplest reading of "clears on fully- or partially-successful import" that stays internally consistent (failed lines already relocated to the errors box, so clearing primary never loses data).
- Retry recombines `primary.value + "\n" + errorsBox.value` and reprocesses via the same `processImportText` path as Run — matches both retry tests' before/after assertions exactly (fixed line merges and clears from errors; still-bad line remains in errors, no duplicate merge).

No stable module (`import-parser.ts`, `actions.ts`, `model.ts`) needed changes — no bugs found there.
